{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/819997-gadgets-grafts-and-harvesting-cryptids","id":819997,"title":"Gadgets, Grafts, and Harvesting Cryptids","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-30T15:04:05-08:00","id":819997,"title":"Gadgets, Grafts, and Harvesting Cryptids","content":"Is it possible to take a Cryptid, &quot;disassemble it&quot; and create a gadget from thusly acquired materials? I ask because if it were possible, would that mean an Agency could theoretically farm a menagerie of cryptids to build and trade various gadgetry?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T15:14:11-08:00","id":820003,"title":"","content":"There's an Exploit from page 112 of Flowers Of Hell called Living Installation that does just that. You can use the biological tissue of people, animals, cryptids and maybe other supernaturals with ST approval. The resulting Gadgets can only contain Embeds and lasts for month. You get the Willpower dot back if you gain an Exceptional Success, though.<br /> <br /> That being said, I think it's more interesting to allow Living Installation to contain Exploits by including it in a Lambda Gadget.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T00:22:26-08:00","id":820803,"title":"","content":"Not quite, living installation doesn't allow one to turn biological tissue into a gadget, it turns a living creature into a gadget. I imagine that taking a part of that living creature would result in the same thing if you tried that with a nonliving gadget- a broken gadget. <br /> <br /> And honestly, I don't see any benefit whatsoever out of making a gadget out of cryptid parts, since the resulting gadget would have the exact same powers as if one created it out of spare parts from the dump for far less trouble.<br /> <br /> Now if you intended something along the lines of form gadgets for cryptid adaptations, perhaps a lambda gadget of some sort.<br /> <br /> Hellhound/merge to create a scalpel that allows one to cut off cryptid adaptations and attach them to a demon's form perhaps?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T05:21:18-08:00","id":820897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now if you intended something along the lines of form gadgets for cryptid adaptations, perhaps a lambda gadget of some sort.<br /> <br /> Hellhound/merge to create a scalpel that allows one to cut off cryptid adaptations and attach them to a demon's form perhaps?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe something like Ephemeral Cover/Show of Power?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T02:58:50-08:00","id":821519,"title":"","content":"Yes, I could see that working too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T10:37:57-08:00","id":823488,"title":"","content":"That's the fun of Demon: options.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"u